{
    "version": "1.5.8-master-7a3657a0aa7e",
    "description": "A native Windows-first, BusyBox-style POSIX shell and utility bundle. Nightly build from master.",
    "homepage": "https://github.com/xiongnemo/nemosh",
    "license": "Apache-2.0",
    "notes": [
        "This is a prerelease built from master. For the stable line install nemosh instead.",
        "nemosh is a multicall binary: only the nemosh shim is installed, because two of its applets would shadow Windows commands of the same name and different meaning -- find.exe takes a literal string and a file, and sort.exe is not POSIX sort.",
        "Run 'nemosh --list' to see the bundled applets, and 'nemosh --help' for the command line.",
        "Like a POSIX shell's, the rc file and history stay in your home directory: ~/.nemoshrc and ~/.nemosh_history. Completion specs are kept in %USERPROFILE%\\.config\\nemosh\\completions (XDG_CONFIG_HOME moves them).",
        "Completion specs in %APPDATA%\\nemosh\\completions, and history that nightlies 1.5.2 and 1.5.3 left in .local\\state\\nemosh, keep working from there. To move them, close the other nemosh windows and run 'nemosh --migrate --dry-run', then 'nemosh --migrate'."
    ],
